{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789218131,"nonce":"ctiPRbZzDeFosp6CWl+zg4OowTU=","title":"A branch made from the wrong block when its condition short-circuits","message":"Lowering `a and b` / `a or b` builds a diamond and leaves control in\nits merge block, recorded in continuation_block. Both the ternary\nexpression and the CFG CondBranch terminator then wrote their own\nterminator into the block they started in, overwriting the diamond's\nentry edge. The diamond was orphaned and the branch read a value\ndefined in a block nothing reached: Cranelift panics with \"no entry\nfound for key\" at the CondBranch. This is the `if a \u003c b \u0026\u0026 b \u003e 3` panic\npreviously noted as pre-existing.\n\nThe Jump terminator arm already redirected through continuation_block;\nthe CondBranch arm and the ternary did not.\n\nReproducer: `x if 0 \u003c= x \u003c= 10 else 10` and `while n \u003e 0 and steps \u003c\n100`.","files":null}]}